# Walkthrough - Cloning Superpowers

I have successfully cloned the `superpowers` repository from GitHub into the workspace.

## Changes Made

### Repository Cloned
- Cloned `https://github.com/obra/superpowers` into `c:\projects\claude+antigravity`.
- Cloned `https://github.com/ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills` into `c:\projects\claude+antigravity\awesome-claude-skills`.

### Key Skills & Features Identified
- **superpowers**: A toolkit for TDD, brainstorming, and systematic debugging.
- **awesome-claude-skills**: A curated list of 30+ practical skills for document processing, dev tools, marketing, and more.
- **frontend-design**: A skill for creating production-grade, distinctive frontend interfaces avoiding "AI slop" aesthetics.
- **connect-apps**: A plugin to connect Claude to 500+ apps via Composio.

### OpenCode CLI Installed
- Installed `opencode-ai` via npm (version 1.2.27).
- Configured Superpowers plugin by linking `superpowers.js` into `%USERPROFILE%\.config\opencode\plugins`.
- Linked the skills directory into `%USERPROFILE%\.config\opencode\skills\superpowers` using a junction.

### Dedicated car_dash Repository
- Repurposed `projects/car_dash` as a standalone Git repository.
- Created `evatechnosoft/car_dash` on GitHub.
- Set up `master` and `dev` branches.

### Futuristic Gauge & Background Integration
- **Interactive Dashboard**: Successfully implemented Speedometer and Battery gauges.
- **Dynamic Background**: Added a speed-reactive particle system ("Warp Drive" effect).
### Automated Dashboard & New Gauges
- **Mock Data Simulation**: Implemented `DashboardController` to simulate real-time speed, SOC, range, and thermal data.
- **Range & Motor Temp**: Added fütüristik vertical bar gauges to track energy and heat.
- **Power Flow Monitor**: Created a dynamic energy flow visualizer (Battery <-> Motor) that reacts to çekiş/regen.
- **UI Autonomy**: Removed the manual slider; the dashboard now breathes and moves on its own like a real vehicle.

### Phase 5+: Advanced Customization & Metrics
- **Expanded Telemetry**: Integrated **Voltage (V)**, **Power (kW)**, and **Controller Temperature** into the simulation engine.
- **On-Dashboard Mini-Settings**:
  - When a gauge is long-pressed (Edit Mode), a small "Edit" icon appears.
  - Clicking this icon opens an overlay to adjust the **Scale** and **Accent Color** in real-time, or to **Delete** the gauge without leaving the dashboard.
- **Restoration (Unset) List**: The Settings screen now intelligently tracks "Available" gauges that aren't on the dashboard, allowing you to add them back with one click.

